  {
    "sha": "f294307a559a6fc565017baa493f89ee580f31c2",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKGYyOTQzMDdhNTU5YTZmYzU2NTAxN2JhYTQ5M2Y4OWVlNTgwZjMxYzI",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T23:27:46Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T23:27:46Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(sim): the lathe field sweeps the blade's own meridian profile\n\nA turning op now cuts the stock field with its tool's true footprint\ninstead of refusing blades by name (LATHE_BLADE_REFUSAL is gone):\n\n- stock_sim::LatheProfile (new field_blade.rs): Nose (the existing\n  stadium, unchanged closed form), Blade (grooving/parting rectangle of\n  its width, corners rounded by corner_r), Thread (the V of its included\n  angle cut off at the crest width), Form (the crown arc across its\n  band, chorded inside the arc within CROWN_SAG_TOL = 1e-4 mm).\n- The sweep of the convex footprint along a chord is the hull of both\n  end copies; its signed distance is closed form, read in the query's\n  meridian at both signs of the radius (parting past centre included).\n- One reading with #103's meridian rapid law: tip at the band's centre,\n  body outward by the tool's flute_len, V widening by tan(angle/2).\n- Stock::simulate_lathe_profile; simulate_lathe(_about) delegate to the\n  nose profile. The lathe entry points moved from backend.rs to\n  field_lathe.rs (400-line law). LathePlan carries the profile; its\n  display feature is the nose or half the blade's band.\n\nPinned by stock_lathe_blade (brute-force stamp reference at cell/20\nsteps: never under-cut, agreement within one step, for a corner-rounded\nplunge groove, a part-off past centre, a two-pass 60-degree thread and a\nform sink; nonsense profiles refused by name) and lathe_field_sim's\na_grooving_blade_cuts_its_rectangle_and_the_verdict_refuses_the_lathe\n(a generated GrooveRough with zero sign misses against the swept\nrectangle). No golden changed.\n\nFixes #21\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
