  {
    "sha": "5a044ce67acb0d0180d15ee443667b43af5c87e8",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDVhMDQ0Y2U2N2FjYjBkMDE4MGQxNWVlNDQzNjY3YjQzYWY1Yzg3ZTg",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-08T11:15:32Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-08T11:15:32Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): refuse helical threading passes by name at plan time\n\nThe Threading kernel writes each pass as half-turn helical arcs about\nthe spindle. The field walk chorded them and LatheSweep::of refused the\nchords as \"skewed off one meridian\" - a geometry blame for what is an\nunsupported program kind; revolving the helix instead would show the\ncrests cut. lathe_plan now refuses, by the op's name and before the\nwalk, any turning program with an arc whose plane does not hold the\nfitted spindle: LATHE_THREAD_REFUSAL for a thread tool,\nLATHE_HELIX_REFUSAL otherwise. Axial (meridian) thread passes still cut\nwith the V footprint.\n\nReview nits: profile_of passes the tool's raw corner_r and form crown\nto the footprint gate (validated at plan time), so a NaN or oversize\ncorner and a band wider than its crown refuse by name instead of being\nclamped or stood in by a rectangle.\n\nThe #21 decision entry moves from RECOMMENDED.md to\ndocs/decisions/21-blade-sweep.md (main's per-file rule), with the\nthread decision added.\n\nPinned by lathe_field_tools::a_generated_threading_op_refuses_the_field_by_name\nand a_generated_form_op_cuts_its_crown_on_the_field.\n\nRefs #21\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
